---
/**
 * Page-specific (getting-started) wrapper for the short "you say" terminal
 * examples. The examples are 2-4 short lines, so the default full-column
 * expressive-code frame leaves a wide empty band at desktop width. This caps the
 * frame at a narrow, left-aligned max-width so it hugs the example text, while
 * the real install/export terminal blocks (outside this wrapper) stay full
 * width. The .gssay class exists only on this page, so the :global rule that
 * reaches the slotted code block never affects another page. No data changes:
 * this only narrows the frame around the same lines.
 */
---

<div class="gssay">
  <slot />
</div>

<style>
  .gssay :global(.expressive-code) {
    max-width: 31rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .gssay :global(.expressive-code) {
      max-width: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
